{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793739450,"nonce":"ZdPEJ9Li+o2eN+rL+oStZtFzbjo=","title":"Keyboard navigation: Tab traversal, Enter/Space activation and a focus ring for pressable controls","message":"Today only the text inputs and a few cn widgets (tree_view, dropdown_menu, calendar, number_gauge, input_otp) take keys. Buttons, checkbox, switch, toggle, radio, tabs, select and the rest have no Tab focus, no Enter/Space activation and no focus ring.\n\nSlice for 0.6.0:\n1. A node can be focusable (tab stop); Tab and Shift+Tab move focus through tab stops in tree order, wrapping.\n2. Enter and Space on a focused pressable dispatch a click.\n3. :focus-visible matches after keyboard focus (not pointer focus); cn rules draw the ring from a token.\n4. cn button, checkbox, switch, toggle, radio and tabs trigger are tab stops; disabled ones are skipped.\n5. Dialog/sheet/drawer trap Tab inside the overlay and restore focus on close (cut if it threatens the release).\n\nOut of scope: arrow-key roving within groups beyond what exists, screen-reader semantics (0.6.1 accessibility item).\n\nTest in blinc_recorder Headless: key(Tab) moves focus, Enter fires on_click, ring appears only after keyboard focus.","files":null}]}